Inconclusive for H1. failcheck's probe thread was blocked for ~58 min in timed_run (subprocess.run waits forever for a child that survives SIGKILL): a probe read started ~114 s in did not die on SIGKILL and ended only near the end of the run. Head kept writing probes (450). node fusectl waiting 2-15, often >= 12 (background slots saturated by slow OSD + socket failures + 8 aggressive readers). Worker D-state episodes 70-115 s, all cleared. Idle check clean (waiting=0). timed_run fixed: polls, abandons a child that survives SIGKILL and reports it (unkillable_probe) with wchan/syscall/stack.
